# Accepted upstream-owned findings — real CVEs in Python dependencies
# resolved by the Hermes installer (mcp 1.26.0, python-multipart 0.0.27,
# starlette 1.0.1). Not patched here: the uv environment is upstream's
# tested set, and this image tracks upstream as closely as possible; the
# fix arrives with a Hermes release. Exposure: MCP/ASGI server-side
# components, and the only server run is the dashboard bound to
# 127.0.0.1:9119 behind the password-gated VNC display — "no known
# remote path", not "proven unreachable".
# Re-evaluate on every HERMES_VERSION bump.
CVE-2026-52869
CVE-2026-52870
CVE-2026-59950
CVE-2026-53539
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283

# Same regime as the entries above, all in the Python environment the
# Hermes installer resolves (uv.lock) or in the CPython build uv ships:
#
# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack 1.1.2 out-of-bounds read, fixed in
#   1.2.1. Only ever decodes payloads the agent produced in the pod.
# CVE-2026-97687 / CVE-2026-97689 — urllib3 2.7.0 (HTTPS-proxy TLS
#   override, chunk-parser DoS), fixed in 2.8.0. No proxy is configured
#   in the image, and the agent's HTTP traffic is its own outbound calls.
# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools 70.3.0 path traversal in PackageIndex,
#   fixed in 78.1.1. It sits in uv's own CPython distribution, not in
#   hermes' venv, and nothing installs packages at runtime: the tree is
#   root-owned and the pod rootfs is read-only.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
CVE-2025-47273
